[ceiling] The pump-bay lintel is the complete fixed roof at z=283.495. It carries the display/ridge storey and leaves 1 mm above the cartridge crown at z=282.495 for withdrawal. This flat roof is retained as a supported face; a corbel extending into the bay would occupy the cartridge's withdrawal envelope. Support topology and build-up require the production slice for this mesh.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
click: x=0.000 y=39.931 z=283.495

[slope] This is the display PCB end-wall/ridge-support face across the bay, not a corbel hung along either adjacent X wall. `_ridge_wall` supplies its complete starting line from the tee wall's crown, and the 45-degree face lays every following line on that support.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
click: x=0.000 y=47.648 z=308.906

[sliver] The pump jack's receptacle carries the same two snap catches as the umbilical's on back-top — the upper tang keeper 1.4 mm proud and the lower latch keeper 1.3 mm proud, exactly `riteav_keystone.CATCH_UPPER` and `CATCH_LOWER`. Each face bounds a catch backed by the receptacle boss on the ridge wall's cavity face; neither is a free strip.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
